{title: Hark, the Voice of Jesus Calling}
{artist: Daniel March / Joseph Barnby}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: hark-the-voice-of-jesus-calling.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Hark_The_Voice_Of_Jesus_Calling-Galilean) and the Cyber Hymnal score (75% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Hark, the voice of [C]Jesus [D]calling,
[Em]Who [C]will [D]go [G]and [A7]work to[D]day?
[G]Fields [D]are [G]ripe and [C]harvests [D7]waiting,
[Em]Who [C]will [D7]bear [G]the [D7]sheaves a[G]way?
[A7]Long and [G]loud [A7]the [D]Master calls [G]us,
[A]Rich re[D]ward He [A7]offers [D]free;
[G]Who [D]will [G]answer, [C]gladly [G]say[B7]ing,
[Em]Here am [G]I, [D7]send me, send [G]me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]If you cannot [C]cross the [D]ocean,
[Em]And [C]the [D]dis[G]tant [A7]lands ex[D]plore,
[G]You [D]can [G]find the [C]lost a[D7]round you,
[Em]You [C]can [D7]help [G]them [D7]at your [G]door;
[A7]If you [G]can[A7]not [D]give your thou[G]sands,
[A]You can [D]give the [A7]widow’s [D]mite;
[G]What [D]you [G]truly [C]give for [G]Je[B7]sus,
[Em]Will be [G]pre[D7]cious in His [G]sight.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]If you cannot [C]speak like [D]angels,
[Em]If [C]you [D]can[G]not [A7]preach like [D]Paul,
[G]You [D]can [G]tell the [C]love of [D7]Jesus,
[Em]You [C]can [D7]say [G]He [D7]died for [G]all.
[A7]If you [G]can[A7]not [D]rouse the wick[G]ed,
[A]With the [D]judgment’s [A7]dread a[D]larms,
[G]You [D]can [G]lead the [C]little [G]child[B7]ren
[Em]To the [G]Sa[D7]vior’s waiting [G]arms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]If you cannot [C]be the [D]watchman,
[Em]Stand[C]ing [D]high [G]on [A7]Zion’s [D]wall,
[G]Point[D]ing [G]out the [C]path to [D7]Heaven,
[Em]Of[C]fering [D7]life [G]and [D7]peace to [G]all,
[A7]With your [G]prayers [A7]and [D]with your boun[G]ties
[A]You can [D]do what [A7]Heaven de[D]mands;
[G]You [D]can [G]be like [C]faithful [G]Aa[B7]ron,
[Em]Holding [G]up [D7]the prophet’s [G]hands.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]If among the [C]older [D]people,
[Em]You [C]may [D]not [G]be [A7]apt to [D]teach,
[G]Feed [D]My [G]lambs, said [C]Christ, our [D7]shepherd,
[Em]Place [C]the [D7]food [G]with[D7]in their [G]reach.
[A7]And it [G]may [A7]be [D]that the child[G]ren
[A]You have [D]led with [A7]trembling [D]hand,
[G]Will [D]be [G]found a[C]mong your [G]jew[B7]els,
[Em]When you [G]reach [D7]the better [G]land.
{end_of_verse}
